  "rounds": {
    "1": {
      "note": "屋企 (uk1 kei2) is the natural Cantonese for 'home' — much more colloquial than the formal 家 (gaa1). To talk about going home, <strong>返屋企</strong> (faan1 uk1 kei2, literally 'return home'). Room names are distinct compounds rather than English-style: 廚房 (cyu4 fong2, kitchen), 廁所 (ci3 so2, toilet), 客廳 (haak3 teng1, living room). For 'bedroom', most people just say 房 (fong2) — the formal 房間 (fong4 gaan1) sits in writing or service contexts.",
